            // The reference contract preserves credit[reverter]==amount; the buggy one sets it to 0.
            // After withdrawal failure, the invariant is: credit[actor] is either 0 (on success) or unchanged (on failure).
            // For the reverter, the call always fails, so credit must remain > 0.
            assertTrue(c.credit(address(reverter)) > 0, "Credit should be preserved when external call fails");
